invariant: INV-17
file: sha512_hw.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh sha2-equiv
reason: sha384_of_hw returns without wiping the context it hashed in, so its
  dead frame keeps the end of the input and the digest's words.
  HMAC-SHA-384 hashes a key longer than a block through this call, and
  the bytes left are the key's last ones and the value HMAC then uses as
  its key. The digest is still right, so no vector sees it.
  bin/sha2_equiv_test copies the stack below one sha384_of_hw call and
  looks for two 64-bit words in a row that the call computed from its
  input. The script runs the arm64 binary under qemu-aarch64. The lane
  skips without docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than
  caught.

--- old
    sha384_final_hw(&s, out);
    ct_wipe(&s, sizeof s);
--- new
    sha384_final_hw(&s, out);
